{
  "readme": "G-2 taxonomy contract corpus (ADR 0077 §1, plan §F1 T1.1). Real GPW/NewConnect report-document title shapes (owner's live DB, 2026-07-09, issuers: CBF, CDR, TXT, SWG, MBR + shapes from the report_diff golden corpus) hand-labeled with the expected doc_kind. classify_doc_kind must reproduce every label — the contract test reddens on any marker edit that flips a known-good classification (the 'denylist rot' defect class). url is empty when the URL carries no classification signal; a few rows keep real URLs (companion extensions, the bankier mis-association bug shape). Extend by appending labeled rows; never relabel to make a failing change pass. 2026-07-31 (#270): appended the English auditor-product shapes (review report, independent auditor's/auditors' report, audit report, assurance/attestation report — issuers ORLEN, PKO BP, Pekao, KGHM, XTB, BDX) plus the auditor-SELECTION negative that keeps the new markers from over-firing. Same change: the two bankier reused-slug rows (ABS/Asseco) pin the title-precedence rule — a URL-only auditor marker must not demote a titled statement — and the DataWalk `Report_on_Review` / KGHM `MB_report_on_activities` rows pin the two title shapes that precedence would otherwise misread. 2026-07-31 (#275): the Asseco and XTB rows now carry their REAL consolidated slugs and stay `periodic_jsf` — title-first precedence extended to the consolidated/standalone axis. 2026-07-31 (#269): systematic marker-dictionary pass — period-cadence families (kwartał/kw./półrocze/śródroczny, quarterly|interim|financial report), the ride-along non-statements that carry a filing's SSF/JSF token (oświadczenie zarządu, SzDZ, selected-data extracts, komentarz/prognoza/szacunki, MAR-19 notifications), convening notices, and the glued-extension title shape; the near-miss negatives (Production-Sales report, SB annual activity report, PZU solvency report, Wyniki finansowe QSr) pin that the new families do not overfire.",
